><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20250709125405+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20250709125407+10'00'" name="fd9b89ec-a1e7-4757-b2b0-c13718456f62" page="6" coords="96.586700,273.236938,336.177704,273.236938,96.586700,263.378082,336.177704,263.378082,84.631790,262.776184,336.176636,262.776245,84.631790,252.917328,336.176636,252.917389,84.631607,252.315506,336.176331,252.315353,84.631607,242.456635,336.176331,242.456482,84.631927,241.854599,336.177185,241.854660,84.631927,231.995728,336.177185,231.995789,84.632202,231.393906,336.176636,231.393845,84.632202,221.535034,336.176636,221.534973,84.631653,220.933090,336.177979,220.933151,84.631653,211.074219,336.177979,211.074280,84.632080,210.472397,336.177429,210.472366,84.632080,200.613525,336.177429,200.613495,84.631531,200.011612,336.178406,200.011551,84.631531,190.152740,336.178406,190.152679,84.631821,189.550797,336.177490,189.550766,84.631821,179.691925,336.177490,179.691895,84.632294,179.090012,336.177734,179.090042,84.632294,169.231140,336.177734,169.231171,84.631760,168.629288,336.177155,168.629257,84.631760,158.770416,336.177155,158.770386,84.631989,158.168503,336.177643,158.168442,84.631989,148.309631,336.177643,148.309570,84.631683,147.707687,336.176605,147.707657,84.631683,137.848816,336.176605,137.848785,84.632278,137.246902,336.177368,137.246964,84.632278,127.388031,336.177368,127.388092,84.632248,126.786194,336.176941,126.786148,84.632248,116.927322,336.176941,116.927277,84.631805,116.325394,336.176758,116.325348,84.631805,106.466522,336.176758,106.466476,84.631744,105.864594,116.209320,105.864594,84.631744,96.005722,116.209320,96.005722" rect="84.323441,95.697632,336.486511,273.545044" subject="Comment on Text" title="Alexander Gibson"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>This is the first comprehensive exploration of support typeand support providers in female cricket players. Regardless ofexpertise levels, there were unique and context-specific roles thatdifferent individuals play in supporting athletes on their sportingdevelopment journeys. Mothers and fathers were primary giversof financial and emotional support, mentors offered meaningfulsport specific informational and technical (or coaching related)support, and siblings and peers played an integral operationalrole in acting as fellow participants for practice and play. Accessto coaching emerged as a dominant point of difference betweencommunity and elite players across all support providers, illustrat-ing that elite players draw on more contact points to aid themin accessing the right type of coaching. The father emerged as adominant provider of support for elite female cricketers, acrossmultiple types of support. This finding should be explored inmore detail in future research in the area of athlete support forfemales.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="6" rect="637.179993,181.236938,821.179993,273.236938"
/></highlight
